red with A3, which lost 6.0 points and swung the lead from Black +2.5 to -3.5. The engine preferred E8. It was the 12k's costliest move, and it handed the edge straight back to Opus 5.5."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered A4 and lost 5.8 points, taking the lead from Black -3.5 to +2.3 and returning the gift. The engine's choice was F8. Within two moves the same advantage had changed hands twice."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "H7 started a run of four moves on the right edge (H7, H8, J8, G8), each losing between 4.4 and 4.8 points. The lead bounced between Black +2.9, +7.2, +2.8 and +7.4 before settling at +2.5. The engine wanted D5 every time, and Opus 5.5 finally played it on turn 46."}, {"turn": 54, "text": "Opus 5.5 passed with the game at Black +2.2, and the 12k passed back. The final position has the 12k's wall on the right and centre against White's long row along the fourth line, and the result stands at B+2."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills the pasted board to print each group's stones and liberties, and count.py counts stones and enclosed territory with named dead stones removed; both only inspect the given position, with no candidate move generation, scoring of moves, or look-ahead.", "stop": false}}